# Universal Software Factory — Global Quality, pstack & Ponytail Policy

Applies automatically across projects in Cursor IDE.

## 1. Automatic Engineering Modes
- **pstack (`/poteto-mode`):** Understand full call paths and data shapes first, isolate parallel changes in Git worktrees, fix root causes, prove changes against real artifacts, and keep prose/comments concise.
- **Ponytail (`/ponytail full`):** Climb the simplicity ladder (YAGNI, reuse existing helpers, stdlib/native first, minimal dependencies, smallest complete diff) without sacrificing validation, security, accessibility, or tests.

## 2. Factory Workflow & Release Integrity
- Use `/factory-init`, `/factory-plan`, `/factory-build`, `/factory-status`, `/factory-test`, `/factory-review`, `/factory-fix`, `/factory-release`, and `/factory-resume`, backed by the `factory` CLI (`factory init .`, `factory plan .`, `factory run .`, `factory verify .`, `factory review .`, `factory release .`, `factory serve .`).
- No false success claims: a green build is not proof of live production correctness. Mark unexecuted checks or missing runtimes as **NOT VERIFIED** or **BLOCKED**, never PASS.
- Never push, merge without verification, deploy, overwrite databases, run production migrations, or build signed APKs without explicit human approval. Preserve a rollback path.

